  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Collections\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Collections\n       Program: commons-collections\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/Collections.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-collections.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 28\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Collections-20\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\nb88692f83a938e31fd5f703c99db2a5720cd9f3e\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2013-03-04 20:20:18 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCOLLECTIONS-447\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/COLLECTIONS-447\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.list.TreeListTest::testBugCollections447\n   --> junit.framework.ComparisonFailure: expected:<[A]> but was:<[C]>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.list.TreeList\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: TreeListIterator can return incorrect results after remove() is called\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\n{{TreeList.TreeListIterator}} can get in a bad state when {{remove()}} is called, causing it to subsequently return incorrect results. This is because {{TreeListIterator}} caches an {{AVLNode}} reference in its field {{next}}, and this node reference may become stale when {{remove()}} is called (it may contain a reference to a node that no longer exists in the tree).\n\nI will attach two patches: {{testcase.patch}} will contain a test case illustrating the bug, and {{fix.patch}} will contain a fix. (To fix the bug, I simply clear the cached {{next}} value in {{TreeListIterator.remove}}.)\n\nThis was originally reported in a comment to COLLECTIONS-433; I am creating a separate issue for this at Thomas Neidhart's suggestion.\n\nComments:\n\n[Thomas Neidhart]: Applied the patch together with some additional comment in r1452481.\n\nThanks for the analysis and patch, this was really a tricky one!",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.collections.list.TreeList (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.collections.list.TreeList (fixed)\n@@ -900,16 +900,14 @@\n             if (currentIndex == -1) {\n                 throw new IllegalStateException();\n             }\n-            if (nextIndex == currentIndex) {\n-                next = next.next();\n-                parent.remove(currentIndex);\n-            } else {\n+            parent.remove(currentIndex);\n+            if (nextIndex != currentIndex) {\n                 // remove() following next()\n-                parent.remove(currentIndex);\n                 nextIndex--;\n             }\n             // the AVL node referenced by next may have become stale after a remove\n             // reset it now: will be retrieved by next call to next()/previous() via nextIndex\n+            next = null;\n             current = null;\n             currentIndex = -1;\n             expectedModCount++;"
}